Z||000000||Enrico||05-13-99||08:11 PM||||I have a 86 fiero 6 cylinder 4 speed.Just started making noise in all gears(2 wood blocks banging together sound)I have a tranny from a 84 4 cylinder fiero. Will I run into any problems? Any help will be greatly appreciated(I plan on installing it this weekend) <br>                           thanks<br>                             Quad4Racer@aol.com 
Z||000001||PaUL||05-13-99||08:17 PM||||The tranny from the 4 cyl. must be an Isuzu 5spd. It will bolt up to the 2.8 v6 block but you should use a larger diameter clutch, use the one for the v6. Also the shift cables may be different.
Z||000002||ChadMan||05-14-99||06:54 AM||||Are you sure, Paul?  I thought all 4-cyl Fieros had the Isuzu 5-sp EXCEPT the 1984's, which had the same X-car 4-sp as the 1985-86 V6 cars.  <p>My first Fiero was a 4-sp 1984 Coupe, and its transmission & cable routing looked identical to my 1986 4-sp SE V6.  So I think you're in luck, Enrico (though I have no idea whether the clutch itself is different).
